these performers are Holograms every  series we take one step closer to  achieving all of the sci-fi dreams that  I've ever dreamed of  it's pretty cool you'll never have to  miss a gig again the gig can come to you  we travel to Paris to meet Ian O'Connell  director of the company that put this  show on I recall we were being asked to  produce a show from London to Florida  where the interaction between the  musicians and the audience would be as  natural as two people being in the same  room and for all of us it was an  experience that we'll never forget  so how do they beam this band in live  it's incredible that this really is a  remote live gig the signal from London  takes less than a third of a second to  go all the way around the world and be  projected as a hologram on the stage in  the US as well as the hologram making it  feel like the band are actually in the  room with the audience the band can see  the audience and actually interact and  respond to what they're doing this is a  whole new take on live music but how are  the image is so good that it looks like  the band are really on stage they look  so lifelike because of the angle of the  light and the reflective material called  mylar that creates this holographic  effect the mylar screen is  semi-transparent the reflective surface  reflects the images where the light  falls on it but where the light doesn't  fall on it the audience can see through  it so it looks like there's a person  standing on the stage and that there is  no screen at all the projector receives  the video signal and projects it down  from the ceiling it hits a bounce screen  on the floor which then reflects the  light back up into the mylar which  reflects it at a 45 degree angle into  the audience so if you have something  horizontal on the floor and a reflecting  surface at 45 degrees the final image as  you see here on stage is going to appear  perpendicular what I really love about  this is that if you get the effect of a  3d hologram without  stupid glasses I still believe we've  only scratched the surface with this  technology I think we will see pop-up  Holograms everywhere that's it the  Holograms are here we're officially in  the future
 

